# interplay_versions_efi_3: EFI and the driver's version: the firmware's framebuffer comes up before any version (_features all zero, nothing tears it down), then the driver writes its version: 0 and 2 (no efiDisplay) tear EFI down and zero its registers, 3 and 245 keep it presenting; 2 then 245 cannot bring it back. A guest at 2 that enables EFI after its version write keeps it (the flag is checked only at a version write), and a migration then restores it on the fresh device (rvg_device_did_resume replays the EFI registers after rvg_device_will_resume set version 2) until the guest writes its version again. Each driver then connects port 0, presents, turns EFI off and presents again.
